<title>USA: Renaissance preliminary Q1 EPS $0.23.</title>
<headline>Renaissance preliminary Q1 EPS $0.23.</headline>
<dateline>LINCOLN, Mass. 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Renaissance Solutions Inc on Tuesday released preliminary first-quarter financial results that included earnings per share of $0.23 and revenues of $17.5 million.</p>
<p>The company also named William Jenkins its chief financial officer, replacing George McMillan.</p>
<p>McMillan, who was also chief operating officer, is leaving to become president and chief executive of BMG Direct, New York, a division of Bertelsmann AG.</p>
<p>Jenkins was formerly vice president of finance and administration for Renaissance.</p>
<p>McMillan has been working with Renaissance during his transition, and will participate in the company's conference call when it releases its detailed quarterly results on Wednesday, Renaissance said.</p>
</text>
